SECTION 2: MANDATORY HUMANITARIAN SAFEGUARDS & PROHIBITIONS
================================================================================

The permissions granted in Section 1 are immediately void, revoked, and terminated 
ab initio if the software or any of its algorithmic derivatives are utilized in 
violation of any of the following clauses:

2.1 Absolute Prohibition of Harm
This software, its algorithmic components, tensor fields, verification routines, 
and diagnostic scripts must never be used, directly or indirectly, by any entity 
to design, simulate, optimize, test, operate, or deploy systems intended to cause 
physical harm, bodily injury, or death to human beings, or the destruction of 
civilian infrastructure.

2.2 Strict Non-Weaponization Mandate
The mathematical primitives and code assets contained within this repository shall 
not be integrated into, or used in conjunction with, any offensive or defensive 
kinetic targeting systems, launch-vector planners, hyper-adversarial strike layouts, 
target-selection engines, or autonomous weapon swarm orchestration substrates. 
Use of this software by any military entity, state department of defense, or 
defense-industrial contractor for active weapon system development or deployment 
is explicitly prohibited.

2.3 Protected Spheres of Passive Defensive Deployment
Live system deployment of this architecture is strictly limited to peaceful, non-military, 
passive protective environments. Valid operational domains are limited to protecting 
civilian transportation networks, public energy grids, water distribution infrastructure, 
medical logistics networks, and open-science human-centered computing utilities 
from structural defects, data corruption, or external physical hazards.

